- Typography/colors/layout are aligned with the requested - Core requirement met: preview now uses a dedicated SF.gov-style component (`SfGovPagePreview`) with static header/nav/search and footer columns/social/seal treatment, and is wired into the right-side preview in `App.tsx`.
design direction: Rubik/Roboto Mono Google Fonts added in `index.html`; preview uses SF palette tokens (`#002B48`, `#5A7A92`, `#495ED4`, white), and an ~800px centered content column.
- Page structure is implemented: page type label with underline, large title, summary block, and cleaner section headings (no old card/icon section header treatment).
- Related links are rendered in arrow-row style and visually match the requested pattern.
- Builder/tool UI remains separate; the SF styling is scoped to the preview region.

Non-blocking issues worth noting:
- Section renderer does not appear to implement explicit table parsing/styling or checklist-specific rendering; these will currently degrade to plain paragraphs/lists rather than SF-native table/checklist patterns.
- Inline link parsing (e.g., markdown links inside paragraph text) is not explicitly handled, so “blue underlined links” is only partially satisfied (button/action links and related rows are styled, but generic inline links are not).
- Minor fidelity nit: font import includes extra weights (500/700) beyond requested set; not functionally harmful.

Security:
- None observed (no authz/input-handling/security-sensitive changes in scope).

Next actions (high-impact):
1) Add minimal markdown/table/checklist parsing in `renderSfGovLines` so tables/checklists render in SF-native styles.
2) Add inline link detection/rendering (markdown `[text](url)` and raw URLs) with SF action-blue underline styling.
